config SENSOR_AFE4400
	bool "Enable AFE4400 driver"
	default y
	help
		Enable the AFE4400 PPG sensor driver (async RTIO-capable)

if SENSOR_AFE4400

config AFE4400_PRF_HZ
	int "AFE4400 pulse repetition frequency / PPG sample rate (Hz)"
	default 250
	range 62 2000
	help
	  PPG sample rate, in Hz. This is the single source of truth for the rate:
	  the driver programs PRPCOUNT = (4000000 / PRF) - 1 from the AFE4400's
	  4 MHz timer clock, and the application derives HPI_PPG_RATE_HZ from this
	  symbol, so the advertised rate and the hardware can no longer disagree.

	  Every DATA_READY assertion is one PPG sample, so this directly sets the
	  sample-bus rate, the SPI load to the ESP32, the rate the M4 sees (after
	  the 2:1 decimation in platform/ipc.c, which adapts automatically) and the
	  ppg_rate field written into .HP6 recordings.

	  250 Hz is the HealthyPi 6 design rate. 125 Hz is also valid -- usable PPG
	  content sits well inside that -- and halves bus, SPI and recording load.

	  Only the repetition period changes with this option. The LED, ambient and
	  ADC-convert phase timings are deliberately left fixed, so the tuned LED
	  currents, TIA gain and R-ratio behaviour are identical at any rate; a
	  slower PRF simply idles longer between identical acquisitions (which also
	  lowers average LED power). The acquisition pattern occupies counts 0..1650,
	  which bounds the maximum PRF; PRPCOUNT is a 16-bit field, which bounds the
	  minimum.

endif # SENSOR_AFE4400
